    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1075-a1">

                <pb facs="1163" n="1067" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1067"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 126.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">senate chamber.</hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">[Joint Resolution No. 1.]</p>
                <p>The Legislature of the Republic of Hawaii, in regular session assembled, does
                    hereby extend to the United States of America its deep and earnest sympathy in
                    the great loss of life sustained by the destruction of the battle ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> in the harbor of Habana, Cuba, February 15,
                    1898.</p>
                <pb facs="1164" n="1068" xml:id="pg1068"/>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That a copy of these resolutions be
                    presented to the American minister for transmission to the President of the
                    United States of America.</p>
                <p>February 26, 1898.</p>
                <p>Approved this 4th day of March, A. D. 1898.</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sanford P. Dole</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">President of the Republic of Hawaii.</hi></p>
                <p>I hereby certify that the foregoing Resolution No. 1 passed in the Senate of the
                    Republic of Hawaii by a unanimous vote, this 26th day of February, A. D.
                    1898.</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. C. Wilder</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">President.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">George Manson</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Clerk.</hi></p>
                <p>I hereby certify that the foregoing Resolution No. 1 passed in the House of
                    Representatives of the Republic of Hawaii by a unanimous vote, this 26th day of
                    February, A. D. 1898.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Lot Kanlukon</hi>, <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Speaker.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jas. N. K. Keola</hi>, <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Clerk.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
